                <pb facs="0707" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115/14100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-15T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                                1918—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>786. It having become impracticable for Nielsen to proceed to London, Department
                    desires you to address a communication to Foreign Office in sense of
                    Department’s telegram No. 180, July 12, beginning with words: “The Department
                    has given careful consideration”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
